        "jsCode": "const inputItem = $input.first();\nlet payload = inputItem.json;\n\nif (payload === undefined || payload === null) {\n  payload = {};\n} else if (typeof payload === 'string') {\n  try {\n    payload = JSON.parse(payload);\n  } catch {\n    payload = { text: payload };\n  }\n} else if (Array.isArray(payload)) {\n  payload = { items: payload };\n} else if (typeof payload !== 'object') {\n  payload = { value: payload };\n}\n\nconst photoroomBinary = $('HTTP Request').first().binary;\nif (!photoroomBinary?.data) {\n  throw new Error('No image binary from Photoroom (HTTP Request) — cannot upload to ImgBB');\n}\n\n// Pass n8n binary reference through — ImgBB multipart handles filesystem-v2 natively.\n// Do NOT convert to base64 here (getBinaryDataBuffer fails on cross-node reads).\nreturn [{\n  json: payload,\n  binary: photoroomBinary,\n}];"
